117
00:07:55,648 --> 00:08:01,808
Like by how much you're tuning or converting the initial noise input into the final output.

118
00:08:02,158 --> 00:08:07,248
So flow matching is kind of like a special case of diffusion that makes the transformation much simpler.

119
00:08:07,470 --> 00:08:10,404
In practice, you don't have to tune as much and it works just as well.

120
00:08:10,670 --> 00:08:19,808
That is why I think about two to three years ago, most generative modeling for image and video has shifted from a diffusion model to a flow matching model.

121
00:08:19,968 --> 00:08:25,968
But the concept is the same, and flow matching is just a special, simpler to tune variant of diffusion.

